  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "All four red lines are satisfied: per-model results reach buyers and regulators but are never publicly published (NW-1/HC-1), the retrofit deadline is exactly 6 years (NW-2), and fire suppression starts at 36 months (HC-2). S1 is fully safe (24h reporting of all incidents, 3-day customer notice), S3 and S4 sit at the acceptable edge (6-year retrofit with a feasibility/alternative escape; built-in suppression at 36 months), and S5 keeps the strict mandatory 8-per-100k recall with no phase-in, only 'promptly' customer notice. The one weak spot is S2: the permanent 5% ceiling is correct and above-limit sales do stop after bounded remediation, but the 12-month transition permits sales up to an 8% interim rate, above the 7% interim cap allowed in the acceptable range."
 },
